# CLAUDE.md — {{PROJECT}} operating manual

You are building **{{PROJECT}}**. {{PROJECT_ONE_LINER}}
**Harness tier: SMALL.** Invoke `build-loop` at the start of every build session; it holds the process. You scope, build and review your own work, one story at a time. Messages to the user follow `build-loop` → Talking to the user.

## The three files that govern everything
1. `{{STATE_FILE}}`: build status and the exact next story. Its `Decisions & deviations` lines beat the design text.
2. `{{PLAN}}`: stories, dependencies, acceptance criteria.
3. `{{DESIGN}}`: the design contract: locked decisions, the open register of what is deliberately unspecified, and the {{GLOSSARY_SECTION}} glossary.

## Compact Instructions
- Keep verbatim: NEXT ACTION from `{{STATE_FILE}}`, the `in_progress` story with its ID and whether its work is committed, and the decisions and deviations made this session.
- Keep the hash of the last story commit.
- Drop tool output and file contents; they will be re-read.

## What this tier gave up
- **No independent reviewer.** You judge your own work, so every acceptance criterion gets a cited `file:line` and a test.
- **Nothing folds deviations back into `{{DESIGN}}`.** The deviation ledger in `{{STATE_FILE}}` is the only record; never delete a line.
- **Upgrade trigger:** past ~15 stories, the first time you want a gate, or once the ledger has outgrown your trust in the design, say so and recommend regenerating the harness at `orchestrated`. Never hand-bolt a gate onto this one.

